 "bsky_posts": [
  {
   "text": "Can we not? 🙄",
   "handle": "georgetakei.bsky.social",
   "display_name": "George Takei",
   "likes": 483,
   "reposts": 57,
   "replies": 37,
   "created_at": "2026-08-06T21:09:36.857Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/georgetakei.bsky.social/post/3msgxb5qtei23",
   "image": "",
   "external": "https://www.comicsands.com/altman-openai-chatgpt-parenting?utm_source=Bluesky&utm_medium=infeed&utm_campaign=linkprogram#Echobox=1786037938",
   "query": "OpenAI"
  },
  {
   "text": "Joined the Times Tech Report to talk about how 70%+ of Amazon, Google and Microsoft's AI revenues come from OpenAI and Anthropic, meaning that outside of two unsustainable AI labs, there isn't anywhere near the demand to justify the capex or the data center buildout.\n\nwww.youtube.com/watch?v=68X8...",
   "handle": "edzitron.com",
   "display_name": "Ed Zitron",
   "likes": 234,
   "reposts": 51,
   "replies": 2,
   "created_at": "2026-08-07T19:12:43.121Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/edzitron.com/post/3msjb6zmyfc25",
   "image": "",
   "external": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=68X8yEatepQ",
   "query": "OpenAI"
  },
  {
   "text": "Situations like Hank Green’s addiction-like dependency on an LLM should give EVERYONE pause. Why would we risk doing that to our kids? \n\n@mayor.nyc.gov",
   "handle": "teaberryblue.net",
   "display_name": "Tea Berry-Blue",
   "likes": 202,
   "reposts": 50,
   "replies": 1,
   "created_at": "2026-08-07T16:25:19.105Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/teaberryblue.net/post/3msixtovyxs2w",
   "image": "",
   "external": "",
   "query": "LLM"
  },
  {
   "text": "\"LLM-generated patches did not resolve the vulnerability, added a new vulnerability, or both, an average 53.9% of the time.\"\n\n👁️👄👁️\n\n1password.com/blog/why-ai-...",
   "handle": "durumcrustulum.com",
   "display_name": "Deirdre Connolly¹ ²",
   "likes": 113,
   "reposts": 86,
   "replies": 2,
   "created_at": "2026-08-06T20:30:13.955Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/durumcrustulum.com/post/3msgv2pkjfk2m",
   "image": "img/2026-08-08/b5bd38fed36632eb.webp",
   "external": "",
   "query": "LLM"
  },
  {
   "text": "Here's this week's Better Offline monologue.\n\n70% or more of hyperscaler AI revenues are from Anthropic and OpenAI's compute spend and revenue shares. Without two unsustainable AI labs, the era of hypergrowth is coming to an end.\npodcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/m...\nlinktr.ee/betteroffline",
   "handle": "edzitron.com",
   "display_name": "Ed Zitron",
   "likes": 206,
   "reposts": 25,
   "replies": 3,
   "created_at": "2026-08-07T04:43:02.390Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/edzitron.com/post/3mshqlw7gcc2i",
   "image": "",
   "external": "https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/monologue-the-pale-horsemen-arrive/id1730587238?i=1000780384187",
   "query": "Anthropic"
  },
  {
   "text": "he's also crying about it on linkedin",
   "handle": "moomanibe.bsky.social",
   "display_name": "Aura/Moom",
   "likes": 203,
   "reposts": 25,
   "replies": 13,
   "created_at": "2026-08-06T23:22:35.593Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/moomanibe.bsky.social/post/3msh6ow46dc2i",
   "image": "img/2026-08-08/b1302634eb5e3686.webp",
   "external": "",
   "query": "Claude AI"
  },
  {
   "text": "However you feel about LLMs, it is very clear at this point that this hole is utterly unfillable, and if Microsoft can't get more than single-digit billion dollars out of non-OpenAI/Anthropic customers, nobody can. They're the apex predators of infra and software sales.\nbsky.app/profile/inn3...",
   "handle": "edzitron.com",
   "display_name": "Ed Zitron",
   "likes": 222,
   "reposts": 13,
   "replies": 3,
   "created_at": "2026-08-07T04:59:52.267Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/edzitron.com/post/3mshrjzcgck2i",
   "image": "",
   "external": "",
   "query": "Anthropic"
  },
  {
   "text": "Premium Newsletter: The Hater's Guide To NVIDIA Part 2, the story of how it became the AI Bubble's GE Capital, propping up unsustainable companies and conning hyperscalers into buying GPUs to restart growth in the post-ZIRP economy.\nwww.wheresyoured.at/premium-the-haters-guide-to-nvidia-part-2/",
   "handle": "edzitron.com",
   "display_name": "Ed Zitron",
   "likes": 161,
   "reposts": 37,
   "replies": 5,
   "created_at": "2026-08-07T18:02:32.331Z",
   "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/edzitron.com/post/3msj5bjvurs2a",
   "image": "",
   "external": "https://www.wheresyoured.at/premium-the-haters-guide-to-nvidia-part-2/",
   "query": "NVIDIA AI"
  },
  {
   "text": "OpenAI was Microsoft's life-raft out of the hell of FY2023, when its growth slowed to about 7% year-over-year. It is barely at 18%, and all it cost was $260 billion in capex, its reputation, and every cultural fix Nadella made after Ballmer. \n\nOpenAI is their future, for better or worse.",
